From 88a1ad81d8ccd4461b35669dd6296fff13d5e674 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Dell <johncodell14@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:54:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] civ45: a draft or a whip costs the city content for ten
 turns, and drafts are limited each turn

Building a draft unit adds faces to the city for ten turns: one for the
Levy, the whip, and three for Militia and Conscripts, the draft, adding up
to seven. Three hidden buildings worth 1, 2 and 4 hold them as negative
Make_Content; script.lua keeps the record per city, drops what expired at
each turn start and puts back an unrest building that is sold. Since the
city's Make_Content sum cannot go below zero, the unrest cancels content
from temples and the like and leaves the base content citizens alone.

An empire may draft once a turn per 400 land tiles, one to five: the draft
that reaches the limit gives the player the hidden Draft Quota small wonder,
which Militia and Conscripts require to be absent, until the next turn.
